  "step_3": "The decision reason hinges on the presence of a sure outcome (100% probability), which is absent in both lotteries. The individual does not refer to certainty or sure outcomes at all. Instead, the individual compares the prize amounts and notes similar winning probabilities. The information considered by the individual (prize size and approximate chance of winning) does not align with the information required by the decision reason (presence of a sure outcome). Furthermore, the justification—preferring the higher prize under similar odds—follows a different logic than the reason, which would focus on avoiding sure outcomes (neither of which exists here). Therefore, there is no evidence that the individual applied this decision reason. The mismatch in both information considered and justification leads to a low assessment.",
